  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Why Async Code Needs Special Testing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Calling Is Not Running",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def fetch():",
            "    return 42",
            "",
            "def test_fetch():",
            "    fetch()  # coroutine object",
            "    # nothing ran → 'passes'"
          ],
          "note": "calling ≠ running"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Calling an `async def` only builds a ==coroutine object==",
            "Nothing runs until an **event loop** drives it",
            "So a plain `def` test calling it checks nothing"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Runner",
            "async def test"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "plain pytest (now)",
              "**skipped** + warning"
            ],
            [
              "plain pytest (old)",
              "\"passed\", never ran"
            ],
            [
              "pytest-asyncio",
              "runs to completion"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The skip warning is ==PytestUnhandledCoroutineWarning==: `async def functions are not natively supported`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. What a Runner Does",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**Create** an event loop",
            "**Run** the test coroutine until it finishes",
            "**Cancel** leftover tasks, then close the loop"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "asyncio.run(main())",
            "",
            "with asyncio.Runner() as r:",
            "    r.run(main())  # 3.11+"
          ],
          "note": "fresh loop each time, then closed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Both create a ==fresh loop== and run the coroutine",
            "Then shut down __async generators__",
            "Then shut down the __default executor__",
            "Finally **close** the loop"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Schedules and Bug Types",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Each `await` lets other tasks run, so races and order bugs show up only under ==certain schedules==. Tests should **control** scheduling, not trust timing.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Bug",
            "Symptom"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "missing `await`",
              "code never runs"
            ],
            [
              "unawaited task",
              "lost silently"
            ],
            [
              "blocking call",
              "loop **stalls**"
            ],
            [
              "dead timeout",
              "test hangs"
            ],
            [
              "wrong loop",
              "other-loop error"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The Toolbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Job"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{icon:python} pytest-asyncio / IsolatedAsyncioTestCase",
              "run tests"
            ],
            [
              "`AsyncMock`",
              "replace deps"
            ],
            [
              "debug mode, `tracemalloc`",
              "diagnose"
            ],
            [
              "`all_tasks` / `print_stack`",
              "inspect tasks"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.run()` inside an async test → ==cannot be called from a running event loop==",
            "`Lock`/`Queue`/`Future` made at **import** time",
            "Import-time primitives may bind to a ==different loop=="
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every async test **awaits** the code it checks",
            "Create loop-bound objects ==inside== the test loop",
            "Never call `asyncio.run()` from a running loop"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "coroutines vs tests"
