    {
      "page_title": "pytest-asyncio: Markers and Modes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is pytest-asyncio",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`pip install pytest-asyncio` adds an ==asyncio runner== to pytest",
            "Mark an `async def` test with `@pytest.mark.asyncio`",
            "Plugin runs the coroutine to **completion** on an event loop",
            "Sync tests in the same file are fine: they never touch the loop"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The two modes",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ini",
          "lines": [
            "[pytest]",
            "asyncio_mode = strict  # default",
            "# asyncio_mode = auto",
            "# pyproject: [tool.pytest.",
            "#   ini_options] same key"
          ],
          "note": "strict is the default; auto is opt-in"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==strict==: only **marked** tests are handled",
            "strict: async fixtures need `@pytest_asyncio.fixture`",
            "strict coexists with {purple:trio} / {purple:anyio} plugins",
            "==auto==: every async test + fixture runs as asyncio, no markers",
            "auto only if asyncio is your **sole** async library"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Marking in bulk",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# whole module:",
            "pytestmark = pytest.mark.asyncio",
            "",
            "@pytest.mark.asyncio  # whole class",
            "class TestApi:",
            "    async def test_get(self): ..."
          ],
          "note": "class marker covers every async method"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Example",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@pytest.mark.asyncio",
            "async def test_fetch():",
            "    got = await fetch(1)",
            "    assert got == {'id': 1}",
            "def test_sync():  # no loop",
            "    assert parse('1') == 1"
          ],
          "note": "sync and async tests mix freely"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Strict vs auto",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "strict",
            "auto"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Markers",
              "required",
              "none"
            ],
            [
              "Async fixtures",
              "`pytest_asyncio`",
              "plain OK"
            ],
            [
              "trio / anyio",
              "**safe**",
              "clashes"
            ],
            [
              "Boilerplate",
              "more",
              "less"
            ],
            [
              "Claims",
              "marked only",
              "every coroutine"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Plain `@pytest.fixture` on an async fixture in strict mode",
            "→ test gets an **un-awaited** coroutine / async generator",
            "Fix: decorate it with `@pytest_asyncio.fixture`",
            "Marker forgotten in strict → test **skipped** with a warning",
            "Skipped ≠ failed: CI stays {green:green}, the test never ran"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Tip: make it fail",
          "text": "`pytest -W error` turns the ==unhandled coroutine== warning into a **failure**, so an unmarked test can't slip through."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "strict vs auto"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Event Loop Scope and Async Fixtures",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What loop_scope Means",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==loop_scope== sets **how long** one event loop lives. The default is `function`, which gives every test a brand-new loop.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "loop_scope",
            "One loop lives for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`function` (default)",
              "each test"
            ],
            [
              "`class`",
              "one test class"
            ],
            [
              "`module`",
              "one .py file"
            ],
            [
              "`package`",
              "one package"
            ],
            [
              "`session`",
              "the whole run"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Tests, Fixtures, Config",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@pytest.mark.asyncio(",
            "    loop_scope=\"module\")",
            "async def test_a(): ...",
            "# every test in the module",
            "# shares this one loop"
          ],
          "note": "marker scope applies to tests"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@pytest_asyncio.fixture(",
            "    loop_scope=\"session\",",
            "    scope=\"session\")",
            "async def pool():  # DB pool",
            "    return await make_pool()"
          ],
          "note": "loop_scope never narrower than scope"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Set `asyncio_default_fixture_loop_scope = function` in pytest.ini / pyproject",
            "pytest-asyncio **0.24+** warns while this is unset",
            "Put expensive resources on a ==long-lived loop==, built once"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Async Generator Fixture",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@pytest_asyncio.fixture",
            "async def client():",
            "    c = await connect()",
            "    yield c          # test runs",
            "    await c.close()  # teardown"
          ],
          "note": "after yield = async teardown"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Code after `yield` is ==async teardown==",
            "It runs on the **same** loop as the setup",
            "It still runs when the test fails"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
