    {
      "page_title": "Loop Mismatches, Leak Checks & Choosing a Scope",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Session fixture + function-loop test → {red:'Future attached to a different loop'}",
            "Fix: **align** the loop_scope values of the test and the fixture",
            "Overriding `event_loop` to change scope: deprecated 0.22, **removed 1.0**",
            "Shared loop: one test's leftover tasks keep running into the next"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@pytest_asyncio.fixture",
            "async def bg():",
            "    yield (tasks := set())",
            "    for t in tasks: t.cancel()",
            "    await asyncio.gather(*tasks,",
            "        return_exceptions=True)"
          ],
          "note": "cancel, then await leftover tasks"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`loop_scope` must be ==at least as wide== as `scope`",
            "The test's loop must match the fixture's loop",
            "Session pool → mark tests `loop_scope=\"session\"` too"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Leak Check in Teardown",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@pytest_asyncio.fixture",
            "async def no_leaks():",
            "    yield",
            "    me = asyncio.current_task()",
            "    rest = asyncio.all_tasks()",
            "    assert rest == {me}, rest"
          ],
          "note": "leftover task = fire-and-forget bug"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Add `autouse=True` to run it for **every** test",
            "Name tasks so failures show `poller`, not `Task-17`",
            "Most useful on a ==shared loop==, where leaks spread"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Picking a loop_scope",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Resource",
            "loop_scope"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "pure logic",
              "`function`"
            ],
            [
              "HTTP client",
              "`module`"
            ],
            [
              "DB pool",
              "`session`"
            ],
            [
              "test server",
              "`session`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Start with `function`. Widen loop_scope only for ==expensive== fixtures, and widen the tests' loop to **match**."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
