    {
      "page_title": "unittest's IsolatedAsyncioTestCase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is it",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==IsolatedAsyncioTestCase== (3.8+): the stdlib runner for async tests",
            "`async def test_*` methods are **awaited** automatically",
            "Each test gets a brand-new event loop, closed afterwards",
            "That per-test loop is the \"__Isolated__\" in the name"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Lifecycle order",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "setUp",
                "sub": "sync"
              },
              {
                "text": "asyncSetUp",
                "sub": "awaited",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "test_*",
                "sub": "awaited",
                "ink": "accent"
              },
              {
                "text": "asyncTearDown",
                "sub": "awaited",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "tearDown",
                "sub": "sync"
              },
              {
                "text": "cleanups",
                "sub": "last",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`addAsyncCleanup(coro_fn, *args)` registers an ==async cleanup==",
            "Cleanups run in **LIFO** order: last added runs first",
            "They still run when the test fails"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The loop you get",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Feature",
            "Behaviour"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "debug mode",
              "`debug=True` always"
            ],
            [
              "slow callbacks",
              "logged, no setup"
            ],
            [
              "never-awaited coros",
              "logged, no setup"
            ],
