      "page_title": "IsolatedAsyncioTestCase Pitfalls & When to Use It",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Async work in `setUpClass`: it is **sync** and runs outside the loop",
            "No class-level async hook exists for shared async state",
            "Expecting state to carry over between tests: each gets a new loop",
            "Fix: build it per test in `asyncSetUp`, or use pytest-asyncio's `loop_scope`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Per-Test Async Setup",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "class T(IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):",
            "  async def asyncSetUp(self):",
            "    self.db = await connect()",
            "    self.addAsyncCleanup(",
            "        self.db.close)"
          ],
          "note": "cleanup runs even if test fails"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Running the Tests",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Runs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`python -m unittest`",
              "stdlib runner"
            ],
            [
              "`pytest`",
