    {
      "page_title": "Mocking Coroutines with AsyncMock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is AsyncMock",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==unittest.mock.AsyncMock== ships in Python **3.8+**",
            "Calling it returns an ==awaitable==, not the value",
            "Awaiting that awaitable produces `return_value`"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "m = AsyncMock(return_value=5)",
            "aw = m('x')   # awaitable, not 5",
            "await aw      # -> 5"
          ],
          "note": "call gives awaitable; await gives value"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. side_effect options",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "side_effect =",
            "On await"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`ValueError()`",
              "**raised**"
            ],
            [
              "`[1, 2, 3]`",
              "next item each await"
            ],
            [
              "`async def f(x)`",
              "awaited with call args"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Await assertions",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`assert_awaited()`: awaited at least once",
            "`assert_awaited_once_with(1)`: ==exactly once==, same args",
            "`assert_any_await(x)` / `assert_has_awaits([call(1)])`",
            "`await_count` = tally, `await_args` = last await's args"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Auto mocks & async protocols",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`patch('mod.fetch')` on an `async def` gives an ==AsyncMock== automatically",
            "`create_autospec(fetch)` on an async fn: AsyncMock too",
            "MagicMock (3.8+) supports `__aenter__`/`__aexit__`, `__aiter__`"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "cm = MagicMock()",
            "cm.__aenter__.return_value = conn",
            "pool.acquire.return_value = cm",
            "it = MagicMock()",
            "it.__aiter__.return_value=[1,2,3]",
            "# async for x in it -> 1, 2, 3"
          ],
          "note": "async with pool.acquire() as conn"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Example: service test",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "fetch = AsyncMock(",
            "    return_value={'id': 1})",
            "assert await service(fetch) == 1",
            "fetch.assert_awaited_once_with(1)"
          ],
          "note": "assert the await, not just the call"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. called vs awaited",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code under test",
            "assert_called",
            "assert_awaited"
