      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Call ≠ await",
          "text": "`call_count` counts calls; `await_count` counts awaits. A ==gap== between them means a **missing** `await`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Plain `Mock`/`MagicMock` for a coroutine: **TypeError**, can't be used in 'await'",
            "`return_value=asyncio.sleep(0)`: await returns the ==coroutine itself==",
            "That coroutine never runs and leaks as **never-awaited** (see p.7)",
            "Fix: `AsyncMock(return_value=0)` and return plain values"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "bad = MagicMock()",
            "await bad()  # TypeError",
            "ok = AsyncMock(return_value=0)",
            "assert await ok() == 0"
          ],
          "note": "AsyncMock plus plain return values"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "10. Which mock when",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Target",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`async def fn`",
              "`AsyncMock`"
            ],
            [
              "`async with x`",
              "`MagicMock` + `__aenter__`"
            ],
            [
              "`async for x`",
              "`MagicMock` + `__aiter__`"
            ],
            [
              "sync fn",
              "`Mock`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "11. Checklist",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Prefer `patch()` / `create_autospec` so signatures are checked",
            "Assert **awaited**, not just called",
            "Return plain values, never coroutine objects",
            "Check `await_args` when arguments matter"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Autospec wins",
          "text": "`create_autospec(fetch)` rejects ==wrong arguments==, so a typo'd call fails **loudly** instead of passing."
        }
      ],
